# Build context exclusions, applied to EVERY app's `COPY . .`.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN SIZE: each apps/<lang>/<app>/ dir IS the content of that app's Gitea
# repo AND the Kaniko build context. Host-built artifacts landing in an image are not just bloat --
# a host `obj/project.assets.json` carries ABSOLUTE HOST PATHS, and an in-container
# `dotnet build --no-restore` will read it and fail or silently use the wrong paths. The same
# applies to a host-built target/ (rust) or node_modules/ (wrong platform binaries).
#
# Measured 2026-08-22, before this file existed: no .dockerignore anywhere in the tree, so every
# COPY . . ingested obj/ (296K), bin/ (144K), node_modules/, target/, __pycache__/ and a
# 13.8 MB unstripped host-built ELF sitting in apps/go/gowebapp/.
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/obj/
**/bin/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# VCS + editor noise
.git/
**/.gitignore
**/*.swp

# Never ship secrets or operator-local state into a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
bundle/
